From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:20:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The application menu is set before the platform starts

macOS takes the application menu when the platform starts; finding none of
ours then, Avalonia put its own with "About Avalonia" and never looked again.
The "Show ClassicAssist" menu is now set from the App constructor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
---
 ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs b/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs
index cdf6dc3..1760fec 100644
--- a/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs
+++ b/ClassicAssist.Avalonia/App.axaml.cs
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ public class App : Application
     public App()
     {
         Name = "WispUO";
+        WindowKeeper.InstallMenu( this );
     }
 
     public override void Initialize()
